<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<document>
    <properties>
        <title>REST module for Workflow plugin</title>
    </properties>
    <body>
        <section name="REST module for Workflow plugin">
            <subsection name="Overview">
                <p>
                    This module provides REST web services to access to
                    workflow's plugin data.
                </p>
            </subsection>
            <subsection name="Configuration">
			<p>
				Configure the private key for the signature in the file
				<strong>webapp/WEB-INF/conf/plugins/workflow-rest.properties</strong> :
			</p>
			<div class="source">
<pre>
workflow-rest.security.activated=true
workflow-rest.requestAuthenticator.name=signrequest.HeaderHashAuthenticator
workflow-rest.requestAuthenticator.cfg.hashService=signrequest.Sha1HashService
workflow-rest.requestAuthenticator.cfg.signatureElements=
workflow-rest.requestAuthenticator.cfg.privateKey=<strong>change me</strong>
</pre>
			</div>
			<p>
				A client signs a call with two headers :
			</p>
			<div class="source">
<pre>
Lutece-Request-Timestamp: &lt;epoch in milliseconds&gt;
Lutece-Request-Signature: sha1( &lt;private key&gt; + &lt;timestamp&gt; )
</pre>
			</div>
			<p>
				The signature is lowercase hexadecimal. signatureElements is empty, as it was in v7, so the
				signature covers the private key and the timestamp only and binds to no request content. Filling
				it in would change what every existing client has to sign.
			</p>
			<p>
				The check can be turned off with workflow-rest.security.activated=false in the same file, which
				serves <strong>every</strong> call unchecked, doAction included. It exists so the test JSP can be
				driven locally ; leave it on otherwise.
			</p>
			<p>
				The check is bound to the module's four resource classes : WorkflowRest, StateRest, ActionRest and
				ResourceWorkflowRest. A resource class added later without that binding is served unauthenticated,
				and nothing in the build reports it.
			</p>
            </subsection>
        </section>
        <section name="Usage">
            <subsection name="Test JSP">
                <p>
                	There is a JSP that allow to run test on the module-workflow-rest.
                	It is accessible through the following link :
                </p>
                <p>
                	<strong>jsp/admin/plugins/workflow/modules/rest/TestWorkflowRest.jsp</strong>
                </p>
                <p>
                	<strong>Note : </strong>The page needs the right <em>WORKFLOW_REST_TEST</em> (menu System). Its forms call
                	the resources and show the answer, but a browser sends no signature: every call is answered an HTTP 401
                	while <em>workflow-rest.security.activated</em> is true (the default).
                </p>
            </subsection>
            <subsection name="URLs syntax for workflows">
            	<h3>Retrieve the information of one or several workflows in format XML or JSON</h3>
            	<p>
            		XML syntax :
            	</p>
            	<ul>
            		<li>To get all the workflows :</li>
            	</ul>
            	<div class="source">
<pre>
http://myhost/mywebapp/rest/workflow
ou
http://myhost/mywebapp/rest/workflow.xml
</pre>
				</div>
				<ul>
            		<li>To get one workflows :</li>
            	</ul>
				<div class="source">
<pre>
http://myhost/mywebapp/rest/workflow/{id_workflow}
ou
http://myhost/mywebapp/rest/workflow/{id_workflow}.xml
</pre>
            	</div>
            	<p>
            		JSON syntax :
            	</p>
            	<ul>
            		<li>To get all the workflows :</li>
            	</ul>
            	<div class="source">
<pre>
http://myhost/mywebapp/rest/workflow.json
</pre>
				</div>
				<ul>
            		<li>To get one workflows :</li>
            	</ul>
				<div class="source">
<pre>
http://myhost/mywebapp/rest/workflow/{id_workflow}.json
</pre>
            	</div>
            </subsection>
